limitations:
- Networks are exploratory, not confirmatory; edges may not represent true causal relationships;
- Centrality measures at temporal level may not reflect contemporaneous level;
- Item selection based on reliability may lead to less informative structures due to content overlap;
- Patient-level networks are idiosyncratic and not generalizable;
- Time lags between measurements varied, which may affect network structure;
- Multilevel VAR assumes all individuals’ parameters originate from the same distribution, which may not always be realistic.
